{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193552-what-if-a-hero-figured-out-how-anathema-really-work","id":1193552,"title":"What if a Hero figured out how Anathema really work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-09T07:53:32-08:00","id":1193552,"title":"What if a Hero figured out how Anathema really work?","content":"This question is a little too complex for the Simple Question thread, as homebrew could get involved, but I'm still wary about creating a new topic.<br /> <br /> The default still seems to be that Heroes think that Anathema are inherent traits of Beasts, found through their sharp wits. But now with Conquering Heroes, we have Heroes that might actually get the chance to talk with Beasts and learn more about their powers. And the opening fiction for the Player's Guide seems to have a potential Hero arguably purposefully inflicting an Anathema.<br /> Once they know that Anathema are the product of their own imaginations, what happens?<br /> <br /> Perhaps without the sheer force of belief behind them, their ability to inflict Anathema weakens? Conversely, perhaps they can train their ability to inflict them to be more under their control? Perhaps even eventually learning how to attempt to choose what kind of Anathema they inflict (maybe with a Resolve + Occult roll, perhaps as a Gift)? Or at least learning how to instinctively and instantly learn what Anathema they have created (unless they can already do that)?<br /> <br /> And from an OOC perspective, would the ability to choose or instantly discover Anathema be too powerful? Same for the ability to weaken Anathema by successfully convincing a Hero of their true nature (easier said than done)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 03-09-2018, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T08:08:11-08:00","id":1193556,"title":"","content":"Probably going to make them feel awesome. &quot;Holy shit, I can <i>think</i> curses into being! I am so cool!&quot;<br /> <br /> A self-aware Hero is likely to start conjuring Anathema that are convenient by deliberately invoking mythical tropes that just so happen to be what he has on hand; if he knows his target is a Tyrant, a Loremaster might deliberately &quot;discover&quot; an Anathema that impacts her ability to dominate those around her. She a jeweler? There's gotta be some kind of way to link stories of Djinn that binds her to a lamp or something...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T08:17:53-08:00","id":1193562,"title":"","content":"I don't think the &quot;Are you afraid of children?&quot; was a deliberate attempt to place an Anathema. Heroes are simply unaware they draw power from the same source as Begotten, and it'd be hard to convince them otherwise. After all, as far as they know, they 'discover' a weakness that's always been there, and to their mind, this makes a lot more sense than &quot;I, the Hero, give the Monster a weakness&quot;. That's not how the stories go, after all.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I think that even a Hero that IS aware that they are actively putting the Anathema on, they still do so completely unaware, subconsciously - there is no indication they have any control over the process. Can you force your body not to produce urine? Can you stop your fingernails from growing by understanding the process? I'd assume the same holds true for Heroes.<br /> <br /> Of course, in case they could learn how to control that, things would become rather scary rather quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T09:30:06-08:00","id":1193594,"title":"","content":"Well some anathema are probably pretty normal for a hero to think they caused it. The most obvious would be a weak point being an injury inflicted on the monster in a previous encounter. You know like the gap in Smaug's scales being caused by a previous attack on the red dragon. Or a Hero who thinks their magic weapon binds curses into an enemy or something.<br /> <br /> Due to the narrative ties in the Hero V Beast conflict the anathema still needs to make sense. Ie can't make it so Kraken are water soluble, but you could go with the logic that Kraken stories taking place in the ocean mean they're salt water fish and can't breath in fresh water.<br /> <br /> Also looking at the advancement section on 215 of the Beast Corebook it says Heroes only get new gifts by slaying Beasts. So being able learn new ones willy nilly might break things a bit. Upside I will point out that the Anathema rules do mention that Heroes are instinctively aware of the limits and function of an anathema once they place it on Beast. So understanding that they are the cause of an anathema probably wouldn't change too much.<br /> <br /> Also I don't know what we're talking about when we say there was an attempt in the opening fiction. If it's what Wormwood says that was a Nightmare since the user had identified his Horror earlier as the Dead Dog.<br /> <br /> (Also am I the only one who thought Mr. Coffey might turn out to be a Demon due to his name?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-09-2018, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:05:44-08:00","id":1193608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193552-what-if-a-hero-figured-out-how-anathema-really-work?p=1193594#post1193594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I don't know what we're talking about when we say there was an attempt in the opening fiction. If it's what Wormwood says that was a Nightmare since the user had identified his Horror earlier as the Dead Dog.<br /> <br /> (Also am I the only one who thought Mr. Coffey might turn out to be a Demon due to his name?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought the same about the name at first ^^<br /> However, the &quot;You afraid of Kids?&quot; line was uttered by Vince Milliner, who is pretty much definitly a Hero: the Begotten in the story don't see him as Family or anything other than a normal human being (Mr. Coffey specifically says so). Although he seems to be a high-integrity one, debating things like being unable to kill Richard since he's a kid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T06:53:02-08:00","id":1193909,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I was under the impression that high-Integrity Heroes are more aware of their nature and mythic role. Does the new book have anything to say about them and their being conscious of their abilities like Anathema-inflicting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T15:42:07-08:00","id":1194065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193552-what-if-a-hero-figured-out-how-anathema-really-work?p=1193562#post1193562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the &quot;Are you afraid of children?&quot; was a deliberate attempt to place an Anathema. Heroes are simply unaware they draw power from the same source as Begotten, and it'd be hard to convince them otherwise. After all, as far as they know, they 'discover' a weakness that's always been there, and to their mind, this makes a lot more sense than &quot;I, the Hero, give the Monster a weakness&quot;. That's not how the stories go, after all.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I think that even a Hero that IS aware that they are actively putting the Anathema on, they still do so completely unaware, subconsciously - there is no indication they have any control over the process. Can you force your body not to produce urine? Can you stop your fingernails from growing by understanding the process? I'd assume the same holds true for Heroes.<br /> <br /> Of course, in case they could learn how to control that, things would become rather scary rather quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, before they fought, Vince had already observed Mr. Coffey (<b>whom I too thought was a demon until The Stranger got a mention</b>) following the two kids whilst remaining hidden and trying to do things without being noticed, connect that to the idea of how Monsters are weakened or repulsed by innocence, and thus Vince naturally would come to the conclusion &quot;<i>\u200bHe's afraid of kids</i>&quot; with moment he asked the surprised and confused Mr. Coffey being when he placed the Anathema. Heck, Mr. Coffey even seems to admit this when he thinks, &quot;[<i>he'd] been made know</i>\u200b&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":17107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","user":"Mangaholic13","date":". 03-10-2018, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17107-mangaholic13","name":"Mangaholic13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T15:56:05-08:00","id":1194071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193552-what-if-a-hero-figured-out-how-anathema-really-work?p=1193909#post1193909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I was under the impression that high-Integrity Heroes are more aware of their nature and mythic role. Does the new book have anything to say about them and their being conscious of their abilities like Anathema-inflicting?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Nothing really on Heroes.<br /> <br /> Presumably something that's being held off on until the STG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:08:35-08:00","id":1194080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193552-what-if-a-hero-figured-out-how-anathema-really-work?p=1194071#post1194071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Nothing really on Heroes.<br /> <br /> Presumably something that's being held off on until the STG.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aww. But I can wait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/ma